    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. i'm just worried about the tradeoff though. like, i see people arguing that raising wages helps the local economy because people spend more, but then i hear from other owners that it just forces them to cut staff or shut down entirely. is there actual data on which one usually happens in more rural spots, or is it just a toss up?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
