    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense, but it feels like a lot of the \"benefit\" people talk about is kinda theoretical. in a small town, if i have to cut two employees just to stay afloat, that's a definitely real problem for my shop and those people right now. is there a way to look at this without just assuming higher wages are always a good thing for the community? it feels like the \"local demand\" argument ignores the actual struggle of staying in business.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
