      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are correct that focusing solely on aggregate \"local demand\" can ignore the very real, immediate impact on individual businesses and employees. A more nuanced view examines the *type* of business you operate—service vs. product, high vs. low margin. If your business has thin margins driven by low initial operating costs, the direct impact of mandated wage increases will disproportionately feel like a survival threat, regardless of broader local spending trends.",
